;;; An hrule whose `:match` reads a stored negation, `(not (paid ?g))`, stops a debug build —
;;; M1f **W85**, register row `W85/hrule-reads-not`, filed by S1f.7.2 (T1f.7.2.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two guests, of whom Bob is known not to have paid, `(not (paid Bob))`, and an
;;; hrule that supposes a guest owes where it is known they have not paid.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The hrule matches Bob alone, so H is `(owes Bob)` and R is two states, ∅ and
;;; {(owes Bob)}: the goal has no row in the first and `?g = Bob` in the second, which
;;; the `:expect` states. `ein oracle` answers the same R.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ──────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `55aadd0b`, release: this R, exit 0, and the claim holds. A build with debug
;;; assertions stopped where `ein solve` took H, exit 101, on the same assertion.
;;; One answer from both builds since S1f.7.2 (T1f.7.2.3).

(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(relation owes Guest :why "{?1} owes")
(not (paid Bob))
(hrule suppose ()
  :match  (and (is-a ?g Guest) (not (paid ?g)))
  :assert (owes ?g)
  :why "suppose {?g} owes: they have not paid")
(query :goal (owes ?g) :expect (or (model) (model (owes Bob))))
